    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d361-a1">

                <pb facs="0649" n="517" xml:id="pg517"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Appendix A—Paraphrase]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Draft</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Message to Supreme Commander, Allied Expeditionary
                        Force and Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The London Munitions Assignments Board is being authorized to assign surrendered
                    or captured enemy matériel in the hands of British or American-commanded forces
                    in Austria and Germany to the forces of those countries employed in furtherance
                    of the agreed strategy in the war against Japan. After the dissolution of Supreme Headquarters, Allied
                    Expeditionary Force, the respective Chiefs of Staff will issue instructions to
                    the commanding officers of the British and United States zones of occupation
                    with respect to treatment of enemy materiel which is in excess of the
                    requirements of the military commanders and in excess of the matériel needed to
                    fill the requirements of the London Munitions Assignments Board.</p>
                <p>The above message is in reply to 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Scaf</hi>
                     447, which is being repeated to the Supreme Allied Commander,
                    Mediterranean, today.</p>
            </div>
